DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Interval");

$fun_2 = Formula("((sqrt(x)))^2");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((e^(x)))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-9, -4, 1, 10} U (((({-4, -1, 5}) U {-4, -1, 5})) U ({-4, -1, 5}))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(7, infinity) U {-4, -1, 5} U {-9, -4, 1, 10} U (7, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-9, -2, 1, 5, 6, 10} - {-9, -2, 1, 5, 6, 10})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(1, infinity) U {-9, -2, 1, 5, 6, 10} U (1, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("((1, infinity) - (1, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`11+4+16+4*13`]? [_____]{answer=>83,width=>6}
---

[`17+8-10*8`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(-55.),width=>9}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -2, 1, 5, 6, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-4, -1, 5\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, -4, 1, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup ((((A) \cup A)) \cup (A)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`C \cup A \cup B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, -3, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, 5, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 10, -5, -9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -3, 10>") . Compute("<10, -5, -9>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, 5, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, -3, 10>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -5, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 5, -6>") . Compute("<5, -3, 10>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, -6, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 4, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, 10, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -6, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, 10, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 10, 4>") x Compute("<10, -6, 1>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, -6, 1>") x Compute("<7, 10, 4>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 4, -7>") x Compute("<10, -6, 1>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-3, 4, -7>"))}

---

Given this function:

[`[$fun_1]`]

Compute:
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}

---

Given this function:

[`[$fun_2]`]

Compute:
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
